{# narrative_engine/plot_slot — who, where or what fills one slot of a step.
   Asked by PlotPlanning::FillSlots for each slot with more than one
   candidate. The answer is a candidate key, c1 onward.
   Receives: mastermind { name }, scheme, step (the step's sentence with
     each unfilled slot shown as its name in brackets), slot (the name
     being filled), kind (person, place or thing), options [{ key, line }].
   NOTE: no fenced blocks and no literal braces anywhere in this file. #}
[ state scheme ]
{{ mastermind.name }} is working toward this: {{ scheme }}
[ end state ]

[ state step ]
{{ step }}
[ end state ]

[ question pick choice ]
{% if kind == "place" %}Where should [{{ slot }}] be in the step in `step`, to best serve the scheme in `scheme`?{% else if kind == "thing" %}What should [{{ slot }}] be in the step in `step`, to best serve the scheme in `scheme`?{% else %}Who should [{{ slot }}] be in the step in `step`, to best serve the scheme in `scheme`? Prefer the person this scheme is plainly about, if they are on the list.{% endif %}
[ criteria ]
{% for o in options %}{{ o.key }}: {{ o.line }}
{% endfor %}[ end criteria ]
[ end question ]
